+ * vnvm: the compile queue. A TB that reached the threshold waits here (its
+ * export slot holds VNVM_TB_QUEUED, it keeps running on TCI) until the batch
+ * is full or enough TBs have been dispatched meanwhile, then all of them
+ * become one function. tb_flush() drops the queue: the TBs are gone.
+ *
+ * The group function (param $ctx) -> i32:
+ *   locals; env/stack prologue; idx = ctx->idx
+ *   loop $G
+ *     block $Bn ... block $B1 block $B0
+ *       br_table idx [B0 .. Bn-1] Bn
+ *     end  TB0 (loop; if (bp == 0) ... end; end; unreachable)
+ *     end  TB1
+ *     ...
+ *     end  unreachable
+ *   end
+ *   unreachable
+ * TB k is nested in n-k blocks, so its jumps to other TBs of the group
